# UI craft — Kairos Notebook

When changing app, extension, or landing UI, read and obey [`design-system/kairos/MASTER.md`](design-system/kairos/MASTER.md) (source of truth). Tokens: `app/src/styles.css` `:root`; components: `app/src/notebook.css`.

## Must

- One subject per screen; lists of hairline rows, not card grids.
- One highlighter (`--hl`) per screen: a marker swipe, the focus block (`--hl-soft`), or the primary button's offset shadow.
- Primary button: ink with `3px 3px 0 var(--hl)` that snaps flat on press. Secondary: sheet + hairline.
- Gabarito for all UI type; Caveat only for decorative margin notes (`aria-hidden`, info repeated in text).
- Sentence case; plain dates ("Thu, Sep 24 at 10:00 AM MDT", `app/src/format.ts`).
- Light, Dark, High contrast (`app/src/theme.ts`); reduced motion honored; 44px targets; focus ring `--pen`.
- Never name or assume a school in product UI; the school comes from onboarding.

## Must not

- Uppercase eyebrows, numbered `01/02` indexes, middle-dot metadata chains, em-dashes in UI copy.
- Glass/blur, gradients, glow, dark sidebar on a light page, colored left-border cards, mascots or faces.
- Fabricated testimonials, avatars, or counts on the landing page.
